  "_about": "a wild turkey tom: the big body in dark bronze plumage, every feather edged black and glossed copper and green; the bare head blue and red, the red snood hanging over the bill and the red wattle under the chin, the caruncles down the neck; the beard of black bristles from the breast; the barred white-and-dark flight feathers, the rounded tail tipped chestnut; long pinkish legs. Variants: display (the tail raised upright in its fan), hen (smaller, duller, no snood or beard); coat: the white domestic (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints.",
